Subject: [PATCH 10/47] v4.6-gpu: expand infinity_stats with new GPU
 observability counters

Add four new counters to infinity_stats for diagnosing GPU scheduling
behavior and cross-scheduler coupling effectiveness:

  - Idle compensation: triggered when proportional idle compensation
    (0007) activates for a returning-from-idle entity.
  - CPU->GPU coupling: triggered when futex_waiting or cpu_ema == 0
    reduces the entity's effective_total (0008).
  - GPU->CPU coupling: triggered when gpu_passovers accelerate CPU
    EMA decay (0009).
  - Lock drain rounds: triggered when pending_gpu_ns is drained under
    rq->lock (0006).

Buffer increased from 1536 to 4096 and dynamically allocated via
kmalloc to avoid stack frame warnings.

New per-entity dump is deferred to a future iteration to avoid
architectural coupling between infinity_sched.c and DRM scheduler
internals.

