The divergence diagnostic bumped the per-CPU counter on every sleep
transition where |ema_pct - util_pct| exceeded 50 percentage points.
EMA reacts in milliseconds and PELT in hundreds of milliseconds, so a
single transient burst could mint a spurious flag for an otherwise
healthy task.  The counter now fires only after INFINITY_DIVERGENCE_STREAK
(3) consecutive divergent sleeps, filtering single-burst noise and
emitting one bump per divergence episode.  The streak is tracked per
task in struct infinity_ctx and reset on fork.

